<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

<section id="Ax1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Appendix Contents</h3>

</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While our work demonstrates the significant benefits of principled experience management in RLVR, we acknowledge several limitations.
First, since our research scope focused on RLVR, the evaluation tasks are verifiable problems, i.e., mathematical and general reasoning benchmarks where trajectories can be more easily verified as correct or incorrect.
The applicability of our correctness-based bucketing strategy to more open-ended tasks (e.g., creative writing), where rewards are often subjective and dense, remains an open question.
Second, our framework’s definition of a valuable experience is based on heuristics that, while powerful, might be incomplete. ExGRPO might neglect the learning potential of “valuable failures” where some incorrect paths that contain useful training signals <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. This focus on exploitation could risk premature convergence in some scenarios.
Finally, while ExGRPO is built upon a relative policy optimization objective, its interaction with other families of RL algorithms has not been explored.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>The Use of Large Language Models (LLMs)</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We utilize large language models to assist with proofreading, and polishing the text of this paper. The generated responses are treated as decision references and are not adopted wholesale. Importantly, all scientific contributions, conceptual developments, experimental designs, and final decisions were made by human researchers. The outputs from LLMs were treated as references or drafts, subject to human review, modification, and validation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>ExGRPO Algorithm</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> ExGRPO: Experiential Group Relative Policy Optimization</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, experience ratio <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, rollout trails <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, reward model <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize:</span> Policy model <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, experience replay buffer <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, retired set <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each training step <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#999999;" mathcolor="#999999">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#999999;"> Phase 1: Experience Management.</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{E}|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{E}|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Partition <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> buckets <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">last</span> rollout correctness <math id="alg1.l6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbf{1}[r_{k}=1]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbf{1}[r_{k}=1].</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             Obtain sampling probability: <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}=\mathcal{N}(k/K;0.5,\sigma=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}=\mathcal{N}(k/K;0.5,\sigma=1)</annotation></semantics></math> for nonempty <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Calculate experience sampling amount: <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leftarrow\mathsf{min}(\lfloor\rho B\rfloor,|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leftarrow\mathsf{min}(\lfloor\rho B\rfloor,|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             Sample <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> experience: <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{n}\}\sim\mathsf{BukcetSample}(\mathcal{U},\{p_{k}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡𝗎𝗄𝖼𝖾𝗍𝖲𝖺𝗆𝗉𝗅𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{n}\}\sim\mathsf{BukcetSample}(\mathcal{U},\{p_{k}\})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> cf. <a href="#alg2" title="In Details of Bucketed Sampling (). ‣ Appendix C ExGRPO Algorithm ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each experience <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\{e_{1},\ldots,e_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> cf. <math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}{:}\ q^{*}\mapsto\{o^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}{:}\ q^{*}\mapsto\{o^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
               <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each experience trajectory <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}\in e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}\in e</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
                Compute trajectory entropy under <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(o_{i};\pi_{\theta})=-\tfrac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{i}^{t}|q^{*},o_{i}^{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(o_{i};\pi_{\theta})=-\tfrac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{i}^{t}|q^{*},o_{i}^{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
               <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
               Select the trajectory with the lowest entropy: <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}\leftarrow\arg\min_{e\in\mathcal{E}}H(o_{i};\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}\leftarrow\arg\min_{e\in\mathcal{E}}H(o_{i};\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             Experiential policy optimization data <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}\leftarrow\{(q^{*},o^{*})\}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}\leftarrow\{(q^{*},o^{*})\}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
             On-policy optimization data <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}\leftarrow\{q\}^{{B{-}n}}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>on</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}\leftarrow\{q\}^{{B{-}n}}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}\leftarrow\emptyset,\ \mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}\leftarrow\{q\}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>on</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}\leftarrow\emptyset,\ \mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}\leftarrow\{q\}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#999999;" mathcolor="#999999">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#999999;"> Phase 2: Experiential Policy Optimization.</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
            Construct batch data: <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\leftarrow\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>on</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\leftarrow\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}\cup\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sample <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
            
            
             Generate rollouts: <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{o_{1},\ldots,o_{K}\}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{1},\ldots,o_{K}\}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|q)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{o_{1},\ldots,o_{K-1}\}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|q^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{1},\ldots,o_{K-1}\}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|q^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
            
            
             Compute rewards and success: <math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}=\{R(q,o_{j})\}_{j=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}=\{R(q,o_{j})\}_{j=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s=\sum_{j=1}^{K}\mathbb{I}[r_{j}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\sum_{j=1}^{K}\mathbb{I}[r_{j}=1]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l26.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> All successful
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}\cup\{q\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}\cup\{q\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l27.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Add to retired set
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l28.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l28.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Partial success
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
            
            
               Record experience: <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}[q]\cup\{o_{j}~|~r(o_{j})=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}[q]\cup\{o_{j}~|~r(o_{j})=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">32:</span>
            
            
            Compute advantage and update policy model with Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.2 ExGRPO: Experiential Policy Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">33:</span>
            
            
            Remove well-learned samples: <math id="alg1.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}\setminus\{q:q\in\mathcal{S}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}\setminus\{q:q\in\mathcal{S}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">34:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">35:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> Optimized policy model <math id="alg1.l35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overview of ExGRPO (<a href="#alg1" title="In Appendix C ExGRPO Algorithm ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ExGRPO organizes training into two phases: <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">experience management</em> and <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">experiential policy optimization</em>. In first phase, the replay buffer <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is partitioned into buckets based on the most recent rollout correctness <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}(q)</annotation></semantics></math>, and a Gaussian weighting centered at <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> biases sampling toward medium-difficulty problems.
From these buckets, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\min(\lfloor\rho B\rfloor,|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\min(\lfloor\rho B\rfloor,|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math> experiences are drawn, and for each, the trajectory with the lowest entropy under the current policy is selected as <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
These anchors form the experiential sub-batch <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the remaining slots are filled with on-policy samples <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>on</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{on}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the second phase, each batch item generates <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts (or <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{-}1</annotation></semantics></math> plus the past trajectory), rewards are computed, and prompts achieving full success are retired, while partially successful ones refresh <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. The policy is updated using objective in Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.2 ExGRPO: Experiential Policy Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Details of Bucketed Sampling (<a href="#alg2" title="In Details of Bucketed Sampling (). ‣ Appendix C ExGRPO Algorithm ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This sampler first normalizes probabilities <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> over non-empty buckets, then draws bucket counts <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math> using a sequential-binomial implementation of the multinomial distribution, ensuring <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}c_{k}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}c_{k}=n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of samples to be drawn.
Within each bucket, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> items are sampled uniformly without replacement.
This preserves the intended inter-bucket bias (e.g., Gaussian weighting by accuracy) while remaining unbiased within buckets.
The method assumes <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\leq|\mathcal{U}_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\leq|\mathcal{U}_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> for feasibility.
In practice, to handle rare edge cases where a bucket becomes empty, clipping and redistributing the sampling counts will be applied in such scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{BucketSample}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡𝗎𝖼𝗄𝖾𝗍𝖲𝖺𝗆𝗉𝗅𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{BucketSample}()</annotation></semantics></math>. Bucketed Multinomial &amp; Within-Bucket Uniform Sampling</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Valid buckets <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\{(\mathrm{Acc},\{e\})\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Acc</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\{(\mathrm{Acc},\{e\})\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>; probabilities <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}\in[0,1]^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}\in[0,1]^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>; sample size <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            probabilities <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}\in[0,1]^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}\in[0,1]^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Multinomial</span>(<math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># Note: sample <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{N}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{N}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}=n</annotation></semantics></math></span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Initialize <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\leftarrow(0,\dots,0)\in\mathbb{N}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\leftarrow(0,\dots,0)\in\mathbb{N}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leftarrow n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leftarrow n</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
               Draw <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\sim\mathsf{Binomial}\!\left(m,\tfrac{p_{i}}{1-\sum_{j&lt;i}p_{j}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:5.830em;" width="5.830em"><mi>𝖡𝗂𝗇𝗈𝗆𝗂𝖺𝗅</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\sim\mathsf{Binomial}\!\left(m,\tfrac{p_{i}}{1-\sum_{j&lt;i}p_{j}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
               Update <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leftarrow m-X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leftarrow m-X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> collection of <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
            
</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># Note: sampling within a bucket is uniform <em id="alg2.l13.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">without</em> replacement; requires <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\leq|\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{Acc}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>Acc</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\leq|\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{Acc}}|</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}\sim\operatorname{Multinomial}(n,\mathbf{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Multinomial</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}\sim\operatorname{Multinomial}(n,\mathbf{p})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l14.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Draw all bucket counts in one shot
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{sampled\_items}\leftarrow\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sampled_items</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sampled\_items}\leftarrow\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg2.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\leftarrow\mathsf{UniformSample}(\mathcal{U}_{k},\,c_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿𝗈𝗋𝗆𝖲𝖺𝗆𝗉𝗅𝖾</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\leftarrow\mathsf{UniformSample}(\mathcal{U}_{k},\,c_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Without replacement.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{sampled\_items}[\mathcal{U}_{k}]\leftarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sampled_items</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sampled\_items}[\mathcal{U}_{k}]\leftarrow S</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\texttt{sampled\_items},\;[])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sampled_items</mtext><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\texttt{sampled\_items},\;[])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Complexity.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experience management in ExGRPO is efficient. Per step, ExGRPO performs <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(BK)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(BK)</annotation></semantics></math> reward evaluations and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(BK)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(BK)</annotation></semantics></math> likelihood computations.
Bucket partitioning and sampling are <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(|\mathcal{E}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|\mathcal{E}|)</annotation></semantics></math> for bucketization (amortized) and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(K+n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(K+n)</annotation></semantics></math> for drawing counts and items.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Correctness and Constraints.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The procedure assumes <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}\leq|\mathcal{U}_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}\leq|\mathcal{U}_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> for all nonempty buckets. In practice, this is satisfied with high probability when (i) the support of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> excludes tiny buckets or (ii) we clip <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{U}_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{U}_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> and redistribute any deficit to remaining buckets. We adopt the simple feasibility requirement as stated in <a href="#alg2" title="In Details of Bucketed Sampling (). ‣ Appendix C ExGRPO Algorithm ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for clarity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical Notes.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We renormalize <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> over <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">nonempty</em> buckets before sampling; this avoids assigning mass to empty buckets. The scheme is streaming-friendly and yields <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(K)</annotation></semantics></math> arithmetic plus the cost of within-bucket draws. When used in ExGRPO, setting <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}\propto\mathcal{N}(k/K;\mu,\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}\propto\mathcal{N}(k/K;\mu,\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> provides a tunable curriculum over the rollout correctness spectrum. In this paper, we consistently set <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.5,\sigma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.5,\sigma=1</annotation></semantics></math> to align with our analytical findings in <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminaries ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Theoretical Analysis of ExGRPO</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Recap and Formulation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be a query. The rollout (reference) policy is <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the current policy is <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the experiential policy (that produced a replayed trajectory) is <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, form a group <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{q}=\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{q}=\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{i}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math> and use GRPO’s within-group standardization</p>
<table id="A4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}(o_{i},\mathcal{G}_{q})\;=\;\frac{r(q,o_{i})-\mu_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}}{\sigma_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}},\quad\mu_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}r(q,o_{i}),\ \ \sigma_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}=\text{Std}\big(\{r(q,o_{i})\}_{i=1}^{K}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}(o_{i},\mathcal{G}_{q})\;=\;\frac{r(q,o_{i})-\mu_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}}{\sigma_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}},\quad\mu_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}r(q,o_{i}),\ \ \sigma_{\mathcal{G}_{q}}=\text{Std}\big(\{r(q,o_{i})\}_{i=1}^{K}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Based on the practice we detailed in the main body of paper, we follow the simplifications advocated by Dr.GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, removing length and standard deviation normalization. For mixed-policy optimization, we also remove clipping and use policy shaping.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">ExGRPO mixes (i) on-policy groups <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and (ii) <em id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mixed</em> groups <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}}=\{o^{*}\}\cup\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}}=\{o^{*}\}\cup\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> sampled from an experience buffer, where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(\cdot\mid q^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(\cdot\mid q^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!-\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!-\!1</annotation></semantics></math> fresh rollouts come from <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid q^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid q^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. The ExGRPO mini-batch objective (Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.2 ExGRPO: Experiential Policy Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) mixes on-policy and experiential (replayed) contributions with weight <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Per-token importance ratios for a trajectory <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> comparing policy <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to policy <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}</annotation></semantics></math>) are:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(o_{i};\theta,\theta^{\prime}):=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})},\qquad W(o_{i};\theta,\theta^{\prime}):=\prod_{t=1}^{|o|}w_{t}(o_{i,t};\theta,\theta^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(o_{i};\theta,\theta^{\prime}):=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})},\qquad W(o_{i};\theta,\theta^{\prime}):=\prod_{t=1}^{|o|}w_{t}(o_{i,t};\theta,\theta^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We will sometimes write <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> for brevity. For the replayed item <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, ExGRPO uses a bounded <em id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">policy-shaping</em> transform <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)\,{=}\,\frac{w}{w+\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)\,{=}\,\frac{w}{w+\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
instead of hard clipping; this is analogous to truncated/saturated importance ratios in ACER and V-trace, known to control variance at small bias <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Espeholt et al., 2018</a>)</cite>.
We assume bounded rewards, absolute continuity of policies (mutual support overlap), and an auxiliary KL control as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al. (2015)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al. (2017)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumptions.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For formal statements we will use the following standard assumptions where invoked:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A1. Support assumption.</span> For any trajectory <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> produced by a past policy used in replay, <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., target policy has support containing past policy).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A2. Bounded second moment.</span> For any random variable <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> under consideration (rewards, advantages), second moments exist and are finite. Formally, for any policy model <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and query distribution <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\mathcal{D},\,o\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q)}\big[X^{2}\big]&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\mathcal{D},\,o\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q)}\big[X^{2}\big]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">so finiteness of <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees that <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(X)=\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]-\big(\mathbb{E}[X]\big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(X)=\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]-\big(\mathbb{E}[X]\big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A3. Bounded importance ratios.</span> Assume finite trajectory length, there exists <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all relevant trajectories and timesteps,</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{o,t}\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)}\leq m,\quad\text{and hence}\quad\sup_{o}W(o;\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\leq M:=m^{|o|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and hence</mtext><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>o</mi></munder><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{o,t}\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o_{t}\mid\cdot)}\leq m,\quad\text{and hence}\quad\sup_{o}W(o;\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\leq M:=m^{|o|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Unbiasedness of Experiential Gradient</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that, when the replayed trajectory is corrected by the exact per-token importance weight <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the contribution of that trajectory yields an unbiased estimate of the corresponding on-policy term (no bias is introduced by using replay plus exact importance reweighting), even when the advantage <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the full mixed group <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unbiasedness)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption A1, let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}}=\{o^{*}\}\cup\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}}=\{o^{*}\}\cup\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be a mixed group where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> was sampled from <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">past</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> were sampled from <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any measurable function <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> of a trajectory and its group (e.g. <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(o,\mathcal{G})=\sum_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}|q,o_{&lt;t})\cdot\widehat{A}(o,\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(o,\mathcal{G})=\sum_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}|q,o_{&lt;t})\cdot\widehat{A}(o,\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math>), the importance-weighted expectation equals the on-policy expectation:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\mid\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}\big]=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{o}\sim\pi_{\theta}}\big[g(\tilde{o},\tilde{\mathcal{G}})\mid\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">past</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\mid\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}\big]=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{o}\sim\pi_{\theta}}\big[g(\tilde{o},\tilde{\mathcal{G}})\mid\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the right hand side is the expectation with <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by sampling <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{o}\sim\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{o}\sim\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and forming group <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Condition on the other group elements <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is implicit as the sampling of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\mid\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}\big]=\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\mid\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K-1}\big]=\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Further, consider the expectation over <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of expectation, we sum over all possible trajectories (which we denote by <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) weighted by their probability under <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{o^{*}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}}\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o^{*}}\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o^{*})\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\ g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o^{*}}\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o^{*})\big[W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\ g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o^{*}}\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o^{*})\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o^{*})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o^{*})}g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o^{*}}\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o^{*})\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o^{*})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{past}}}(o^{*})}g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E10Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{o^{*}}\pi_{\theta}(o^{*})g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{o^{*}}\pi_{\theta}(o^{*})g(o^{*},\mathcal{G}_{q^{*}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E10Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{o}\sim\pi_{\theta}}\big[g(\tilde{o},\mathcal{G})\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>o</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{o}\sim\pi_{\theta}}\big[g(\tilde{o},\mathcal{G})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The key is that <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\cdot,\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\cdot,\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary measurable function of a trajectory and the group, and the algebra above does not require <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> to be independent of the group statistics (the sum is over the trajectory variable and the group members are treated as constants in the inner sum).
This yields the stated identity.
Thus, we have shown that the importance-weighted experiential term is an unbiased estimator of the on-policy term, conditioned on the rest of the group members.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark.</span> The theorem shows that, with exact importance weights, replay introduces no bias even when the advantage is computed using group-dependent normalization (<math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>). In practice exact per-token ratios are used (product over timesteps), and the identity holds under A1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Variance Decomposition and Bounds</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the random contribution from an experience-mixed group that includes one replayed trajectory corrected by importance sampling as:</p>
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{exp}}\;=\;\frac{1}{K}\Big(W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,U(o^{*},\mathcal{G})+\sum_{i=1}^{K-1}U(o_{i},\mathcal{G})\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>past</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{exp}}\;=\;\frac{1}{K}\Big(W(o^{*};\theta,\theta_{\text{past}})\,U(o^{*},\mathcal{G})+\sum_{i=1}^{K-1}U(o_{i},\mathcal{G})\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(o,\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(o,\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the per-trajectory <em id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unweighted</em> gradient contribution (e.g. <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\cdot)\,\widehat{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\cdot)\,\widehat{A}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Importantly, in our implementation of GRPO the group standard-deviation term is omitted (we only mean-center advantages), so the <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(\cdot,\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(\cdot,\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math> terms still depend on the group mean <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> but not on <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This reduces but does not eliminate the statistical coupling between group members.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Below we give a general variance bound that does not assume independence among group members, and then a tighter bound under a weak-independence assumption that is often approximately valid in practice (e.g., large <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance upper bound for experiential term)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption A2 (finite second moments) and A3 (bounded trajectory importance ratios), the experiential variance satisfies the following bounds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(General, no independence) Without assuming independence between </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(o^{*},\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(o^{*},\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the other group contributions, we have the conservative inequality</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2}{K^{2}}\Big(\mathbb{E}\big[W^{2}U^{2}\big]+(K-1)^{2}\,\mathbb{E}\big[U^{2}\big]\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2}{K^{2}}\Big(\mathbb{E}\big[W^{2}U^{2}\big]+(K-1)^{2}\,\mathbb{E}\big[U^{2}\big]\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If in addition </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is uniformly bounded by </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (Assumption A3), then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2}{K^{2}}\Big(M^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]+(K-1)^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]\Big)=\frac{2\big(M^{2}+(K-1)^{2}\big)}{K^{2}}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2}{K^{2}}\Big(M^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]+(K-1)^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]\Big)=\frac{2\big(M^{2}+(K-1)^{2}\big)}{K^{2}}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A’)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Tighter bound under weak/approximate independence) If the within-group unweighted contributions </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U(o_{i},\mathcal{G})\}_{i=1}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U(o_{i},\mathcal{G})\}_{i=1}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are pairwise uncorrelated and uncorrelated with </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(o^{*})U(o^{*},\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(o^{*})U(o^{*},\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (e.g., approximate when </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is large), then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2}{K^{2}}\Big(\mathbb{E}\big[W^{2}U^{2}\big]+(K-1)\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2}{K^{2}}\Big(\mathbb{E}\big[W^{2}U^{2}\big]+(K-1)\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With the bound </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\leq M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> this yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2\big(M^{2}+(K-1)\big)}{K^{2}}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{2\big(M^{2}+(K-1)\big)}{K^{2}}\,\mathbb{E}[U^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B’)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum_{i=1}^{K-1}U(o_{i},\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum_{i=1}^{K-1}U(o_{i},\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)=\frac{1}{K^{2}}\operatorname{Var}\big(WU+S\big)\leq\frac{1}{K^{2}}\mathbb{E}\big[(WU+S)^{2}\big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)=\frac{1}{K^{2}}\operatorname{Var}\big(WU+S\big)\leq\frac{1}{K^{2}}\mathbb{E}\big[(WU+S)^{2}\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">using <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}(X)\leq\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}(X)\leq\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding and applying </span><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cauchy–Schwarz</span><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text"> to bound cross terms yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{1}{K^{2}}\Big(\mathbb{E}[W^{2}U^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]+2\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[W^{2}U^{2}]\,\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\big(G_{\mathrm{exp}}\big)\leq\frac{1}{K^{2}}\Big(\mathbb{E}[W^{2}U^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]+2\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[W^{2}U^{2}]\,\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+b+2\sqrt{ab})\leq 2(a+b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+b+2\sqrt{ab})\leq 2(a+b)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]\leq(K-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]\leq(K-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> (which follows without independence by bounding pairwise covariances by second moments) gives the general bound (A). Plugging <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{2}\leq M^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{2}\leq M^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> yields (A’).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">If one further assumes pairwise uncorrelatedness of the <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-terms and zero covariance with <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WU" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WU</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]=(K-1)\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[S^{2}]=(K-1)\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> and the cross terms drop, recovering the tighter bound (B) and its specialization (B’).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Practical Remark.</span>
Removing the within-group standard-deviation from GRPO reduces the coupling introduced by a stochastic denominator (the <math id="A4.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-term). This typically lowers <math id="A4.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> compared to the case with standard deviation normalization (because the denominator’s variability can strongly amplify per-trajectory contributions), which in turn reduces all bounds above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the upper bound analysis of variance, an important insight is that controlling the source of experience policy is crucial for reducing the value of <math id="A4.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, and consequently tightening the variance bound. In practice, techniques such as low-entropy selection and importance sampling correction contribute to this goal.
Specifically, we use the average conditional entropy of the trajectory as pickup metric, and minimizing this metric encourages trajectories from the typical set, which facilitates controlling the importance sampling term and reduces the discrepancy between <math id="A4.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Final Remarks</h3>

<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Policy shaping via <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)=\tfrac{w}{w+\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)=\tfrac{w}{w+\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and removing clip.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 ExGRPO: Experiential Policy Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, we remove the CLIP term and replace it with a policy-shaping function to enable better off-policy experience exploitation.
Rather than relying on empirical validation from prior work (use expert trajectory as off-policy), we also provide a discussion of this design choice used in experiential optimization here.
The policy shaping transform replaces <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)</annotation></semantics></math> for the replayed trajectory. Its key properties are:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone increasing in <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq f(w)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq f(w)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For small <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)\approx w/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)\approx w/\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (which can amplify very small ratios when <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>); for large <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and thus damps extremely large ratios.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> reduces variance contribution of large importance weights while introducing bias (since <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[f(W)]\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[f(W)]\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math> generally). Combined with group normalization, medium-difficulty question sampling and low-entropy trajectory, policy shaping often suffices to control variance so that GRPO clipping can be relaxed or removed in practice.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary and Takeaways.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have shown that exact trajectory-level importance weighting guarantees unbiasedness of experiential contributions, even when advantages are computed from mixed groups (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Unbiasedness). ‣ D.2 Unbiasedness of Experiential Gradient ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis of ExGRPO ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). The variance of experiential gradients is governed by the second moment <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[W^{2}U^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[W^{2}U^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, so bounding or controlling importance sampling term is critical (Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 2 (Variance upper bound for experiential term). ‣ D.3 Variance Decomposition and Bounds ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis of ExGRPO ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the smooth policy-shaping transform <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)=\tfrac{w}{w+\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)=\tfrac{w}{w+\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> offers a principled bias–variance tradeoff: it suppresses extreme importance weights while preserving informative contributions that would be truncated by hard clipping. In combination with within-group normalization, this explains why ExGRPO can remain stable without clipping while still benefiting from replayed trajectories.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Supplementary Materials of Experiments</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Detailed Training Settings</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During RLVR training, the rollout generation uses a <span id="A5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">temperature</span> of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
To reduce training time and monitor training dynamics, we used a validation set by sampling 2.2k instances from the test set.
Model performance was evaluated every 10 steps to better track training progress, without applying early stopping.
Qwen2.5-Math 7B backbone was trained for 700 steps, while the models in our extension experiments were trained for 500 steps.
Following the methodology of LUFFY <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we employed a consistent prompt template across all models during training, as detailed in <a href="#A7.SS1" title="G.1 RLVR Training and Evaluation ‣ Appendix G Prompt Template ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>.
An exception was made for the Llama-3.1 8B base model, for which a simplified prompt was used to accommodate its limited capabilities.
Additional training hyper-parameters are provided in <a href="#A5.T2" title="In E.1 Detailed Training Settings ‣ Appendix E Supplementary Materials of Experiments ‣ ExGRPO: Learning to Reason from Experience" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
