<td id="A6.T8.4.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.16</td>
<td id="A6.T8.4.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_border_bb"></td>
<td id="A6.T8.4.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A6.T8.4.5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">56.1</span></td>
<td id="A6.T8.4.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">47.4</td>
<td id="A6.T8.4.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">-8.7</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case Study.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further illustrate this behavior, we present several qualitative examples of such trajectories as follows.
Case #1 presents a challenging question from our training data.
Although all trajectories ultimately arrive at the correct answer, they differ in the soundness and quality of their reasoning chains.
The trajectory with the lowest entropy exhibits a shorter but coherent reasoning process. In contrast, the highest-entropy trajectory allocates more reasoning budget to code verification, producing longer responses that are logically unsound. Upon our inspection, the generated code is also invalid, and the external CoT judge also identifies this trajectory as poor reasoning.
A similar phenomenon is observed in Case #3, which involves an easier problem.
In Case #2, the external judge instead deems the high-entropy trajectory as a correct reasoning chain. However, it still produces unnecessary code in the final step, which we argue is unnatural and misaligned with human-like reasoning behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1588.65" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1588.65" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1588.65) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fg-color:#D9D9D9;" color="#D9D9D9" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.5" stroke="#D9D9D9" stroke-opacity="0.5"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.54 -3.54 L 3.54 1573.92 C 3.54 1580.1 8.55 1585.1 14.72 1585.1 L 542.36 1585.1 C 548.54 1585.1 553.54 1580.1 553.54 1573.92 L 553.54 -3.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#78B4DC;" fill="#78B4DC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 1579.24 C 0 1584.43 4.21 1588.65 9.41 1588.65 L 540.59 1588.65 C 545.79 1588.65 550 1584.43 550 1579.24 L 550 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF7FD;" fill="#EDF7FD" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1.11 L 1.11 1566.26 L 548.89 1566.26 L 548.89 1.11 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#78B4DC;" fill-opacity="1.0" stroke="#78B4DC" stroke-dasharray="2.84528pt,2.84528pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.11 1253 L 548.89 1253"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#92B6D9;" fill="#92B6D9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1567.37 L 1.11 1579.24 C 1.11 1583.82 4.82 1587.54 9.41 1587.54 L 540.59 1587.54 C 545.18 1587.54 548.89 1583.82 548.89 1579.24 L 548.89 1567.37 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6496C8;--ltx-fill-color:#6496C8;--ltx-fg-color:#6496C8;" color="#6496C8" fill="#6496C8" stroke="#6496C8" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 1579.24 C 0.55 1584.13 4.52 1588.09 9.41 1588.09 L 540.59 1588.09 C 545.48 1588.09 549.45 1584.13 549.45 1579.24 L 549.45 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 1573.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="455.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.89em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Case #1 of Snowball Effects</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 1264.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.82em;--ltx-fo-height:20.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="289.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 289.22)" width="523.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.82em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given that <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, and the system of equations</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}x-1988y=n\\
11x+27y=m\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}x-1988y=n\\
11x+27y=m\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">has the solution</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}x=p\\
y=q\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}x=p\\
y=q\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">as integers, then</span></span>
<span id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A)</span> 
<span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are both even.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(B)</span> 
<span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are both odd.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C)</span> 
<span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is even, </span><math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is odd.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(D)</span> 
<span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is odd, </span><math id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is even.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(“Zu Chongzhi Cup” Junior High School Mathematics Invitational Competition, 1988)</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ground Truth:</span><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.2.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 13.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.82em;--ltx-fo-height:88.74em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="1227.85" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1227.85)" width="523.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.3" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.82em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (Low Entropy)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="32.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 507.45 32.23" width="507.45"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#C1E4C1;" fill="#C1E4C1" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.04 L 0 27.18 C 0 29.97 2.26 32.23 5.04 32.23 L 502.41 32.23 C 505.19 32.23 507.45 29.97 507.45 27.18 L 507.45 5.04 C 507.45 2.26 505.19 0 502.41 0 L 5.04 0 C 2.26 0 0 2.26 0 5.04 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 5.04 L 1.11 27.18 C 1.11 29.36 2.87 31.12 5.04 31.12 L 502.41 31.12 C 504.58 31.12 506.35 29.36 506.35 27.18 L 506.35 5.04 C 506.35 2.87 504.58 1.11 502.41 1.11 L 5.04 1.11 C 2.87 1.11 1.11 2.87 1.11 5.04 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.2 12.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="359.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#262626;">Reward<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">1.0</span> </span>Entropy<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.1532</span> </span>CoT Validity (Judged by Qwen3-32B)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Correct.</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To determine the correct answer, let’s analyze the system of equations:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}x-1988y=n\\
11x+27y=m\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}x-1988y=n\\
11x+27y=m\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given that <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, and both <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>) are integers. Let’s substitute <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=q</annotation></semantics></math> to use the equations:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}p-1988q=n\\
11p+27q=m\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}p-1988q=n\\
11p+27q=m\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-1988q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-1988q</annotation></semantics></math> must be even. As <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1988q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1988q</annotation></semantics></math> is always even (since 1988 is even and any integer <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> must also be even for the sum to be even.
Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11p+27q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11p+27q</annotation></semantics></math> must be odd. Since 11p is always odd or even (depending on <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>) and 27q is always odd (since 27 is odd and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>), the sum of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27q</annotation></semantics></math> will be odd if and only if one of them is even and one is odd. Given <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11p</annotation></semantics></math> is even, hence <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27q</annotation></semantics></math> must be odd, implying <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is odd.
So, based on the above reasoning, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is even and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is odd. Therefore, the correct answer is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{(C) }p\text{ is even, }q\text{ is odd.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(C) </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> is even, </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> is odd.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{(C) }p\text{ is even, }q\text{ is odd.}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><code id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;</code></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The final answer is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\text{(C)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(C)</mtext></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\text{(C)}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 523.31 1" width="523.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#92B6D9;--ltx-fill-color:#92B6D9;--ltx-fg-color:#92B6D9;" color="#92B6D9" fill="#92B6D9" stroke="#92B6D9" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -12.24 0 L 535.55 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (High Entropy)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="32.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 502.03 32.23" width="502.03"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#C1E4C1;" fill="#C1E4C1" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.04 L 0 27.18 C 0 29.97 2.26 32.23 5.04 32.23 L 496.99 32.23 C 499.77 32.23 502.03 29.97 502.03 27.18 L 502.03 5.04 C 502.03 2.26 499.77 0 496.99 0 L 5.04 0 C 2.26 0 0 2.26 0 5.04 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 5.04 L 1.11 27.18 C 1.11 29.36 2.87 31.12 5.04 31.12 L 496.99 31.12 C 499.16 31.12 500.93 29.36 500.93 27.18 L 500.93 5.04 C 500.93 2.87 499.16 1.11 496.99 1.11 L 5.04 1.11 C 2.87 1.11 1.11 2.87 1.11 5.04 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.2 12.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="359.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#262626;">Reward<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">1.0</span> </span>Entropy<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.2652</span> </span>CoT Validity (Judged by Qwen3-32B)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Wrong.</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we need to analyze the system of linear equations and determine the parity (even or odd nature) of the variables <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Let’s break it down step-by-step.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the system of equations:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}x-1988y=n\\
11x+27y=m\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}x-1988y=n\\
11x+27y=m\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> are integers, we need to determine the parity of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, let’s express <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. We can use the method of elimination or substitution to solve the system. We can eliminate <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> by multiplying the first equation by 11 and then subtracting the second equation from it:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11(x-1988y)-(11x+27y)=11n-m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11(x-1988y)-(11x+27y)=11n-m</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11x-21868y-11x-27y=11n-m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">21868</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11x-21868y-11x-27y=11n-m</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2215y=11n-m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2215y=11n-m</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\frac{m-11n}{2215}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\frac{m-11n}{2215}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11n</annotation></semantics></math> is even (because any integer multiple of an even number is even). Therefore, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-11n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-11n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd (because odd minus even is odd). Since 2215 is odd, the quotient <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{m-11n}{2215}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{m-11n}{2215}</annotation></semantics></math> will be odd if <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-11n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-11n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd. Hence, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=q</annotation></semantics></math> must be odd.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, we substitute <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=q</annotation></semantics></math> into the first equation to solve for <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=n+1988q" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=n+1988q</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1988q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1988q</annotation></semantics></math> is even (because any integer multiple of an even number is even), the sum of two even numbers is even. Therefore, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=p</annotation></semantics></math> must be even.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So we have:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\text{even},\quad y=\text{odd}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">even</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">odd</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\text{even},\quad y=\text{odd}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, the correct answer is (C) <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is odd.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><code id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.10.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;</code></span><pre id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.11" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">‘‘‘python
# The reasoning above leads us to the conclusion, but we can
verify using a simple Python code snippet to ensure there are no
calculation errors.
# We can test with a few values of n (even) and m (odd) and
verify the results.
import sympy as sp

# Define the variables
x, y = sp.symbols(’x y’)
n = sp.Symbol(’n’, integer=True, even=True)
m = sp.Symbol(’m’, integer=True, odd=True)

# Define the equations
eq1 = sp.Eq(x - 1988*y, n)
eq2 = sp.Eq(11*x + 27*y, m)

# Solve the equations for x and y
solution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2), (x, y))
x_sol = solution[x]
y_sol = solution[y]

# Check the parity of x and y
x_sol_parity = sp.Mod(x_sol, 2)
y_sol_parity = sp.Mod(y_sol, 2)

print(x_sol_parity, y_sol_parity)
‘‘‘
‘‘‘output
Mod(2215*n/2215 - 1988*m/2215 + Mod(1988*m/2215, 2)
Mod(-11*n/2215 + Mod(n, 2), 2)
‘‘‘
</pre>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF5757;">The Python code confirms the parity analysis we performed earlier.<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Here’s the detailed reasoning again with the output from the code:</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. The solution for <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\frac{m-11n}{2215}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\frac{m-11n}{2215}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11n</annotation></semantics></math> is even (because <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even), <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-11n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-11n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd. And because 2215 is odd, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\frac{m-11n}{2215}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\frac{m-11n}{2215}</annotation></semantics></math> will be odd. Therefore, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=q</annotation></semantics></math> is odd.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2.The solution for <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m67" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=11\cdot\left(\frac{m-11n}{2215}\right)+1988n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1988</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=11\cdot\left(\frac{m-11n}{2215}\right)+1988n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m68" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{m-11n}{2215}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2215</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{m-11n}{2215}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is an integer and odd, and 11 times an odd number is odd, and 1988n is even, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=p</annotation></semantics></math> must be even because the sum of an odd number and an even number is odd plus even (which remains even).</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.pic1.p5.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hence, the final answer is:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\text{C}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mtext></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\text{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1481.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1481.54" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1481.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fg-color:#D9D9D9;" color="#D9D9D9" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.5" stroke="#D9D9D9" stroke-opacity="0.5"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.54 -3.54 L 3.54 1466.82 C 3.54 1472.99 8.55 1478 14.72 1478 L 542.36 1478 C 548.54 1478 553.54 1472.99 553.54 1466.82 L 553.54 -3.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#78B4DC;" fill="#78B4DC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 1472.13 C 0 1477.33 4.21 1481.54 9.41 1481.54 L 540.59 1481.54 C 545.79 1481.54 550 1477.33 550 1472.13 L 550 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF7FD;" fill="#EDF7FD" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1.11 L 1.11 1459.16 L 548.89 1459.16 L 548.89 1.11 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#78B4DC;" fill-opacity="1.0" stroke="#78B4DC" stroke-dasharray="2.84528pt,2.84528pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.11 1359.23 L 548.89 1359.23"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#92B6D9;" fill="#92B6D9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1460.26 L 1.11 1472.13 C 1.11 1476.72 4.82 1480.44 9.41 1480.44 L 540.59 1480.44 C 545.18 1480.44 548.89 1476.72 548.89 1472.13 L 548.89 1460.26 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6496C8;--ltx-fill-color:#6496C8;--ltx-fg-color:#6496C8;" color="#6496C8" fill="#6496C8" stroke="#6496C8" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 1472.13 C 0.55 1477.03 4.52 1480.99 9.41 1480.99 L 540.59 1480.99 C 545.48 1480.99 549.45 1477.03 549.45 1472.13 L 549.45 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 1466.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="455.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.89em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Case #2 of Snowball Effects</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 1371.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.82em;--ltx-fo-height:5.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="75.87" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 75.87)" width="523.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.82em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">13. Find the sum:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100-99-98-\ldots-1+1+2+\ldots+101+102" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100-99-98-\ldots-1+1+2+\ldots+101+102</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ground Truth:</span><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.2.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{203}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">203</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{203}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 16.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.82em;--ltx-fo-height:96.21em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="1334.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1331.32)" width="523.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.3" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.82em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (Low Entropy)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="32.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 507.45 32.23" width="507.45"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#C1E4C1;" fill="#C1E4C1" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.04 L 0 27.18 C 0 29.97 2.26 32.23 5.04 32.23 L 502.41 32.23 C 505.19 32.23 507.45 29.97 507.45 27.18 L 507.45 5.04 C 507.45 2.26 505.19 0 502.41 0 L 5.04 0 C 2.26 0 0 2.26 0 5.04 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 5.04 L 1.11 27.18 C 1.11 29.36 2.87 31.12 5.04 31.12 L 502.41 31.12 C 504.58 31.12 506.35 29.36 506.35 27.18 L 506.35 5.04 C 506.35 2.87 504.58 1.11 502.41 1.11 L 5.04 1.11 C 2.87 1.11 1.11 2.87 1.11 5.04 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.2 12.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="359.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#262626;">Reward<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">1.0</span> </span>Entropy<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.2151</span> </span>CoT Validity (Judged by Qwen3-32B)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p1.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Correct.</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find the sum of the arithmetic sequence given by <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100-99-98-\ldots-1+1+2+\ldots+101+102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100-99-98-\ldots-1+1+2+\ldots+101+102</annotation></semantics></math>, let’s break down the problem step-by-step.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Identify the arithmetic sequence:
The sequence is</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1,1,2,\ldots,101,102" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1,1,2,\ldots,101,102</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We can split it into two separate sequences and then find the sum of each:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The first sequence is </span><math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The second sequence is </span><math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2,\ldots,101,102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2,\ldots,101,102</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Sum of the first sequence (<math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1</annotation></semantics></math>):
The sum of an arithmetic sequence from <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> with a common difference of 1 can be found using the formula:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\frac{n}{2}(first\_term+last\_term)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\frac{n}{2}(first\_term+last\_term)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of terms.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For the first sequence:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First term (</span><math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) = </span><math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Last term (</span><math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) = </span><math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Number of terms (</span><math id="A6.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">):</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\frac{l-a}{d}+1=\frac{-1-(-100)}{1}+1=100" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\frac{l-a}{d}+1=\frac{-1-(-100)}{1}+1=100</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I3.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, </span><math id="A6.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=100</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I3.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using the formula:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\frac{100}{2}\times(-100+(-1))=50\times(-101)=-5050" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">50</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5050</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\frac{100}{2}\times(-100+(-1))=50\times(-101)=-5050</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Sum of the second sequence <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,\ldots,101,102)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,\ldots,101,102)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First term (</span><math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) = </span><math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Last term (</span><math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) = </span><math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">102</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Number of terms (</span><math id="A6.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">):</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\frac{102-1}{1}+1=102" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\frac{102-1}{1}+1=102</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=102</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using the formula:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\frac{102}{2}\times(1+102)=51\times 103=5253" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">51</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">103</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5253</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\frac{102}{2}\times(1+102)=51\times 103=5253</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. Combine the sums:
The total sum is the sum of the first sequence plus the sum of the second sequence:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Sum=-5050+5253=203" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5050</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5253</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">203</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Sum=-5050+5253=203</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.12" class="ltx_p"><code id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.12.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;</code></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Answer<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The sum of the arithmetic sequence <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1,1,2,\ldots,101,102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100,-99,-98,\ldots,-1,1,2,\ldots,101,102</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{203}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">203</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{203}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 523.31 1" width="523.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#92B6D9;--ltx-fill-color:#92B6D9;--ltx-fg-color:#92B6D9;" color="#92B6D9" fill="#92B6D9" stroke="#92B6D9" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -12.24 0 L 535.55 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (High Entropy)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p4.14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="32.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 507.45 32.23" width="507.45"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#C1E4C1;" fill="#C1E4C1" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.04 L 0 27.18 C 0 29.97 2.26 32.23 5.04 32.23 L 502.41 32.23 C 505.19 32.23 507.45 29.97 507.45 27.18 L 507.45 5.04 C 507.45 2.26 505.19 0 502.41 0 L 5.04 0 C 2.26 0 0 2.26 0 5.04 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 5.04 L 1.11 27.18 C 1.11 29.36 2.87 31.12 5.04 31.12 L 502.41 31.12 C 504.58 31.12 506.35 29.36 506.35 27.18 L 506.35 5.04 C 506.35 2.87 504.58 1.11 502.41 1.11 L 5.04 1.11 C 2.87 1.11 1.11 2.87 1.11 5.04 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.2 12.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="359.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#262626;">Reward<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">1.0</span> </span>Entropy<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.2967</span> </span>CoT Validity (Judged by Qwen3-32B)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Correct.</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find the sum of the series, we need to break it down into manageable parts. The series is essentially two series combined together, one in descending order from -100 to 102 and the other in ascending order from 1 to 101. We’ll need to sum these series separately and then combine the results.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The series can be split as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. The series <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100-99-98-\ldots-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100-99-98-\ldots-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. The series <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+2+\ldots+101+102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+2+\ldots+101+102</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, let’s look at the series <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100-99-98-\ldots-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100-99-98-\ldots-1</annotation></semantics></math>. This is a single decreasing arithmetic series from -100 to -1. The sequence can be rearranged to form an arithmetic series with a common difference of -1, starting from -100 to -1. The sum of an arithmetic series <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by the formula:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\frac{n}{2}(a_{1}+a_{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\frac{n}{2}(a_{1}+a_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of terms, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the first term, and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the last term.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=-100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=-100</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the number of terms <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=100</annotation></semantics></math>. So, the sum of this series is:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=\frac{100}{2}(-100+(-1))=50\times(-101)=-5050" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">50</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5050</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=\frac{100}{2}(-100+(-1))=50\times(-101)=-5050</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Next, let’s look at the series <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+2+\ldots+101+102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+2+\ldots+101+102</annotation></semantics></math>. This is an arithmetic series starting from 1 with a common difference of 1, ending at 102. The number of terms is 102, so the sum of this series is:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}=\frac{102}{2}(1+102)=51\times 103=5253" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">51</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">103</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5253</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}=\frac{102}{2}(1+102)=51\times 103=5253</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, combine the two results:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Total sum}=S_{1}+S_{2}=-5050+5253=203" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Total sum</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5050</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5253</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">203</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Total sum}=S_{1}+S_{2}=-5050+5253=203</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF5757;">Let’s verify this with Python code.<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.10.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.11" class="ltx_p"><code id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.11.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;</code></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF5757;">Here is the Python code to verify the result:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.12.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span><pre id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.13" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
‘‘‘python
# Sum of the series -100 - 99 - 98 - ... - 1 from -100 to -1
sum_descending = sum(range(-100, 0))

# Sum of the series 1 + 2 + ... + 102 from 1 to 102
sum_ascending = sum(range(1, 103))

# Total sum
total_sum = sum_descending + sum_ascending

print(total_sum)
‘‘‘
‘‘‘output
203
‘‘‘
</pre>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.p5.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The sum of the series <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100-99-98-\ldots-1+1+2+\ldots+101+102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">98</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">101</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100-99-98-\ldots-1+1+2+\ldots+101+102</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{203}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">203</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{203}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="2030.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 2030.15" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,2030.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fg-color:#D9D9D9;" color="#D9D9D9" fill="#D9D9D9" fill-opacity="0.5" stroke="#D9D9D9" stroke-opacity="0.5"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.54 -3.54 L 3.54 2015.42 C 3.54 2021.6 8.55 2026.6 14.72 2026.6 L 542.36 2026.6 C 548.54 2026.6 553.54 2021.6 553.54 2015.42 L 553.54 -3.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#78B4DC;" fill="#78B4DC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 2020.74 C 0 2025.93 4.21 2030.15 9.41 2030.15 L 540.59 2030.15 C 545.79 2030.15 550 2025.93 550 2020.74 L 550 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF7FD;" fill="#EDF7FD" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1.11 L 1.11 2007.76 L 548.89 2007.76 L 548.89 1.11 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#78B4DC;" fill-opacity="1.0" stroke="#78B4DC" stroke-dasharray="2.84528pt,2.84528pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.11 1891.23 L 548.89 1891.23"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#92B6D9;" fill="#92B6D9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 2008.87 L 1.11 2020.74 C 1.11 2025.32 4.82 2029.04 9.41 2029.04 L 540.59 2029.04 C 545.18 2029.04 548.89 2025.32 548.89 2020.74 L 548.89 2008.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6496C8;--ltx-fill-color:#6496C8;--ltx-fg-color:#6496C8;" color="#6496C8" fill="#6496C8" stroke="#6496C8" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 2020.74 C 0.55 2025.63 4.52 2029.59 9.41 2029.59 L 540.59 2029.59 C 545.48 2029.59 549.45 2025.63 549.45 2020.74 L 549.45 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 2015.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="455.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.89em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Case #3 of Snowball Effects</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 1903.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.82em;--ltx-fo-height:6.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="92.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 92.48)" width="523.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.82em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:</span><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## [ Auxiliary area. The area helps to solve the problem ]</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pythagorean Theorem (direct and inverse) In triangle <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math>, heights <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> are drawn. Find the side <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BD=18,BC=30,AE=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BD=18,BC=30,AE=20</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ground Truth:</span><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{25}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{25}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.35 13.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.82em;--ltx-fo-height:134.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="1866.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1866.1)" width="523.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.3" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.82em;">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (Low Entropy)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="32.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 507.45 32.23" width="507.45"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#C1E4C1;" fill="#C1E4C1" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.04 L 0 27.18 C 0 29.97 2.26 32.23 5.04 32.23 L 502.41 32.23 C 505.19 32.23 507.45 29.97 507.45 27.18 L 507.45 5.04 C 507.45 2.26 505.19 0 502.41 0 L 5.04 0 C 2.26 0 0 2.26 0 5.04 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 5.04 L 1.11 27.18 C 1.11 29.36 2.87 31.12 5.04 31.12 L 502.41 31.12 C 504.58 31.12 506.35 29.36 506.35 27.18 L 506.35 5.04 C 506.35 2.87 504.58 1.11 502.41 1.11 L 5.04 1.11 C 2.87 1.11 1.11 2.87 1.11 5.04 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.2 12.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="359.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#262626;">Reward<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">1.0</span> </span>Entropy<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.0198</span> </span>CoT Validity (Judged by Qwen3-32B)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p1.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Correct.</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of right triangles and the Pythagorean theorem. Here’s the step-by-step reasoning:</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Identify the given information:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BD=18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BD=18</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=30</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE=20</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a height from </span><math id="A6.I5.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I5.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="A6.I5.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I5.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, so </span><math id="A6.I5.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD\perp AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⟂</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD\perp AB</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I5.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I5.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a height from </span><math id="A6.I5.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I5.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="A6.I5.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I5.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, so </span><math id="A6.I5.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE\perp BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⟂</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE\perp BC</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Determine the position of point <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>:
Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the foot of the perpendicular from <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BD=18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BD=18</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=30</annotation></semantics></math>, we can find <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math> using the Pythagorean theorem in triangle <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BCD</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD=\sqrt{BC^{2}-BD^{2}}=\sqrt{30^{2}-18^{2}}=\sqrt{900-324}=\sqrt{576}=24" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">900</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">324</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">576</mn></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD=\sqrt{BC^{2}-BD^{2}}=\sqrt{30^{2}-18^{2}}=\sqrt{900-324}=\sqrt{576}=24</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD=24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD=24</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Use the area of the triangle:</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area of triangle <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated in two ways:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using </span><math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I6.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times BC\times AE=\frac{1}{2}\times 30\times 20=300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times BC\times AE=\frac{1}{2}\times 30\times 20=300</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using </span><math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I6.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times 24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times 24</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Equating the two expressions for the area, we get:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times 24=300\implies AB\times 24=600\implies AB=\frac{600}{24}=25" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">600</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">600</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times 24=300\implies AB\times 24=600\implies AB=\frac{600}{24}=25</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, the length of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><code id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.9.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;</code></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The final answer is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{25}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{25}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 523.31 1" width="523.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#92B6D9;--ltx-fill-color:#92B6D9;--ltx-fg-color:#92B6D9;" color="#92B6D9" fill="#92B6D9" stroke="#92B6D9" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -12.24 0 L 535.55 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response:<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (High Entropy)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p4.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="32.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 502.03 32.23" width="502.03"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#C1E4C1;" fill="#C1E4C1" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.04 L 0 27.18 C 0 29.97 2.26 32.23 5.04 32.23 L 496.99 32.23 C 499.77 32.23 502.03 29.97 502.03 27.18 L 502.03 5.04 C 502.03 2.26 499.77 0 496.99 0 L 5.04 0 C 2.26 0 0 2.26 0 5.04 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 5.04 L 1.11 27.18 C 1.11 29.36 2.87 31.12 5.04 31.12 L 496.99 31.12 C 499.16 31.12 500.93 29.36 500.93 27.18 L 500.93 5.04 C 500.93 2.87 499.16 1.11 496.99 1.11 L 5.04 1.11 C 2.87 1.11 1.11 2.87 1.11 5.04 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 9.2 12.65)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="359.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#262626;">Reward<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">1.0</span> </span>Entropy<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.3002</span> </span>CoT Validity (Judged by Qwen3-32B)<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: <span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Wrong.</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of the triangle and the Pythagorean theorem. Here is the step-by-step thought process:</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Understand the Problem:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We need to find the side </span><math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of triangle </span><math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I7.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We know the length of </span><math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BD=18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BD=18</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=30</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I7.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We know the height </span><math id="A6.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE=20</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I7.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Apply the Right Triangle Properties:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since </span><math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a height, </span><math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is perpendicular to </span><math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, so triangle </span><math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AEB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AEB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and triangle </span><math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AEC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are right triangles.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We can use the Pythagorean theorem in triangles </span><math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AEC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I8.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Using the Pythagorean Theorem in <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ABD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ABD</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In </span><math id="A6.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ABD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ABD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I9.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A6.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I9.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can be found using the Pythagorean theorem: </span><math id="A6.I9.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD=\sqrt{AB^{2}-BD^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD=\sqrt{AB^{2}-BD^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I9.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. Using the Pythagorean Theorem in <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEC</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In </span><math id="A6.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A6.I10.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can be found using the Pythagorean theorem: </span><math id="A6.I10.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EC=\sqrt{AC^{2}-AE^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EC=\sqrt{AC^{2}-AE^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since </span><math id="A6.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=BD+DC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=BD+DC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A6.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is on </span><math id="A6.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A6.I10.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DC=BC-BD=30-18=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DC=BC-BD=30-18=12</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In </span><math id="A6.I10.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A6.I10.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=EC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=EC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, because </span><math id="A6.I10.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the height from </span><math id="A6.I10.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="A6.I10.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I10.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5. Using the Area Equivalence:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I11" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area of the triangle can be calculated in two ways:</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I11.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using base </span><math id="A6.I11.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I11.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and height </span><math id="A6.I11.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I11.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><math id="A6.I11.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times BC\times AE=\frac{1}{2}\times 30\times 20=300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times BC\times AE=\frac{1}{2}\times 30\times 20=300</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I11.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.I11.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I11.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I11.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I11.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using base </span><math id="A6.I11.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I11.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and height </span><math id="A6.I11.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I11.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><math id="A6.I11.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I11.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6. Find <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I12" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">From the area equivalence, </span><math id="A6.I12.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD=300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD=300</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I12.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, so </span><math id="A6.I12.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD=\frac{600}{AB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">600</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD=\frac{600}{AB}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I12.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">7. Using the Pythagorean Theorem in <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ACD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ACD</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.I13" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A6.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A6.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In </span><math id="A6.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ACD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ACD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I13.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A6.I13.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=\sqrt{AD^{2}+CD^{2}}=\sqrt{(AB^{2}-BD^{2})+CD^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=\sqrt{AD^{2}+CD^{2}}=\sqrt{(AB^{2}-BD^{2})+CD^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I13.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let’s use these steps to set up the equations and solve for <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><code id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.10.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/think&gt;</code></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using the relationships and the Pythagorean theorem, we can derive the value of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math>. Let’s first find <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> using the properties of the triangle and the given values. We know:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BD=18,BC=30,AE=20" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BD=18,BC=30,AE=20</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, we calculate <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD=\frac{600}{AB}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">600</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD=\frac{600}{AB}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, we use the Pythagorean theorem in <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ABD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ABD</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD=\sqrt{AB^{2}-18^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD=\sqrt{AB^{2}-18^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">And in <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEC</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=\sqrt{12^{2}+20^{2}}=\sqrt{144+400}=\sqrt{544}=4\sqrt{34}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">144</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">400</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">544</mn></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">34</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=\sqrt{12^{2}+20^{2}}=\sqrt{144+400}=\sqrt{544}=4\sqrt{34}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area using base <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> and height <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times 30\times 20=300" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times 30\times 20=300</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The area using base <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> and height <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times\frac{600}{AB}=300" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Area</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">600</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Area}=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times CD=\frac{1}{2}\times AB\times\frac{600}{AB}=300</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus,</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD=\frac{600}{AB}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">600</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD=\frac{600}{AB}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We now use the Pythagorean theorem in <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ABD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ABD</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEC</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD=\sqrt{AB^{2}-18^{2}}=\sqrt{AB^{2}-324}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">18</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">324</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD=\sqrt{AB^{2}-18^{2}}=\sqrt{AB^{2}-324}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=\sqrt{12^{2}+20^{2}}=4\sqrt{34}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">34</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=\sqrt{12^{2}+20^{2}}=4\sqrt{34}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math> is the hypotenuse of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEC</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=AE^{2}+EC^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=AE^{2}+EC^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We can now solve for <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> by equating the areas and solving the equations.</span></span>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF5757;">Let’s now calculate the value of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF5757;" mathcolor="#FF5757">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF5757;" mathcolor="#FF5757">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> using Python to find the accurate result.<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.21.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span><pre id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.22" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">‘‘‘python
import sympy as sp

# Define the variables
AB = sp.Symbol(’AB’, positive=True)

# Given values
BD = 18
BC = 30
AE = 20

# Calculate CD using the area equivalence
CD = 600 / AB

# Calculate AD using the Pythagorean theorem in triangle ABD
AD = sp.sqrt(AB**2 - BD**2)

# Calculate AC using the Pythagorean theorem in triangle AEC
AC = sp.sqrt(12**2 + AE**2)

# Using the area equivalence, CD = AE * BC / AB, we already have
CD = 600 / AB
# Now we solve for AB using the Pythagorean theorem in triangle
ABD and AEC
# We know AC = sqrt(AD^2 + CD^2) and AD = sqrt(AB^2 - 324)
AC_from_AyDC = sp.sqrt((AB**2 - 324) + (600 / AB)**2)

# Equate AC from both triangles since they are the same
equation = sp.Eq(AC, AC_from_AyDC)

# Solve for AB
AB_value = sp.solve(equation, AB)
print(AB_value)
‘‘‘
‘‘‘output
[25]
‘‘‘
</pre>
<span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.p5.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The value of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the final answer is:</span></span>
<span id="A6.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{25}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">25</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{25}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
